WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.210
- [Mark] Alright, Matt and Megan.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.073
Where are you guys,

00:00:04.073 --> 00:00:05.333
where are you guys from, originally?

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.977
- [Matt] I'm originally
from Indianapolis, Indiana.

00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:10.236
- [Megan] And Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.

00:00:10.236 --> 00:00:12.230
- [Mark] Pittsburgh. And,

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.910
how was your childhood?

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.110
You had both parents, one parent?

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:16.943
- Yeah, I,

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.200
grew up in a very nice family.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.973
Both my parents are still married.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.190
I have a younger brother.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.771
You know,

00:00:29.771 --> 00:00:31.950
I had both sets of
grandparents growing up.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.993
Pretty much was able to do whatever,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.408
you know, I wanted to do.

00:00:37.408 --> 00:00:38.241
- [Mark] You had a great childhood.

00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:39.200
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.353
Played sports, played
hockey my whole life.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.720
My brother played hockey,

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.150
traveled a lot as a family.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.073
So yeah, it was a really good childhood.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:51.990
- [Mark] Megan how about you?

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:55.370
- Yeah same, I have both
parents also still married.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.080
I have a huge family, actually.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:58.810
Eight brothers and

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.113
three sisters.

00:01:00.113 --> 00:01:02.550
(Megan chuckles)

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.243
Yeah. Suburban area.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:07.850
Yeah.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.050
I graduated high school.

00:01:10.091 --> 00:01:12.271
- [Mark] And how did you
guys end up down here?

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.104
This is like,

00:01:13.104 --> 00:01:15.830
this is the the opposite
of the spectrum from

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.663
your childhood.

00:01:16.663 --> 00:01:17.496
- That's a good question.

00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:19.170
We ask ourselves that every day.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.800
- Yeah.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.633
Well...

00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:23.410
- [Mark] Is there
addiction in your family?

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.170
- No, there's not.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.790
- I mean, they drink a little bit, but

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.340
not so much, like, you know.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.583
- Yeah. There's no drug use in my family.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.283
Maybe a little bit of alcohol, but,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.693
nothing with drugs.

00:01:41.308 --> 00:01:44.008
- [Mark] When did you guys
first get into using drugs?

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:45.923
- At a very,

00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:47.373
at a very young age for me.

00:01:48.395 --> 00:01:49.228
At

00:01:49.228 --> 00:01:50.061
like

00:01:50.061 --> 00:01:50.894
12.

00:01:50.894 --> 00:01:52.323
I was introduced to just like alcohol,

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.450
but around my freshman
year of high school,

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:56.773
So like 14,

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.670
I was introduced to pills and

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.020
marijuana,

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.976
and more alcohol.

00:02:04.976 --> 00:02:05.809
(Matt coughs)

00:02:05.809 --> 00:02:07.480
And then it just kind of
progressed from there.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.723
My sophomore year,

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.250
I started doing a lot of cocaine

00:02:14.224 --> 00:02:16.090
and,

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:19.286
ecstasy in my junior year.

00:02:19.286 --> 00:02:20.119
(Matt clearing throat)

00:02:20.119 --> 00:02:20.952
And then,

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.420
I was actually sent to

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.810
boarding school my senior
year of high school,

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.143
all the way out in Utah.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.720
And, when I came back from Utah,

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.883
that's when I was introduced
to heroin for the first time.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.600
- Mine was more so after high school,

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.100
I always smoked pot.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.960
No during high school, but

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.523
never really anything hardcore.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.384
Yeah, after high school, it
was pills obviously first.

00:02:48.384 --> 00:02:49.801
And then, heroin.

00:02:51.068 --> 00:02:53.090
- [Mark] And was it your heroin addiction

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.620
that got you guys together?

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.220
Is that how you met?

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.303
- Yeah, so,

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.910
we both came out here

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.630
for rehab.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.456
We both came out here...

00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:06.420
- To Orange County.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.003
- Yeah, to Orange County first, for rehab.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.950
And

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.783
I,

00:03:12.783 --> 00:03:13.616
I went through...

00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:15.430
- [Mark] Coming from Indiana and...

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.520
- Yeah, they flew,

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.340
they flew us,

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.570
both out here.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:20.403
They, you know,

00:03:20.403 --> 00:03:21.270
fly you out here.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.310
- Not knowing each other yet.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.740
- Yeah we didn't know each other yet,

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.090
but they paid for everything,

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:27.730
you know, beautiful places,

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.113
like nice rehabs.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.403
And I kind of bounced from
one to another, to another.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.430
And,

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.080
I was in the middle of a relapse,

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.220
when I met Megan.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.840
And Megan was still in treatment

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:44.793
when I met her.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.340
So. Yeah.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.260
- [Mark] And what are you
guys doing for money now?

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.220
You're living on the
street, in a tent, right?

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.890
- Yeah. We live in a tent.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.461
- [Mark] Yeah. What do you do for money?

00:03:56.461 --> 00:03:57.294
- Boosting.

00:03:57.294 --> 00:03:58.643
- Yeah. We boost, we steal.

00:04:00.175 --> 00:04:01.810
- From stores.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:02.643
- Yeah.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.320
Our parents send us
money every now and then.

00:04:07.965 --> 00:04:08.963
- [Mark] Your parents
know you're out here?

00:04:08.963 --> 00:04:12.640
- Our parents know that
we're in California,

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.460
in Los Angeles, but not that we're

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.030
living in a tent.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.200
My, both of our parents would be

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.250
absolutely horrified to...

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.400
- They wouldn't believe it.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.110
- Yeah, they wouldn't
even believe it, honestly.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.960
Both of our parents are kind of aware that

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.503
we're not doing exactly
what we're supposed to,

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.360
but, you know,

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.113
they don't know the severity of it.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.710
So, yeah.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.610
- [Mark] What does your addiction
cost you in like a week?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.950
- I,

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.640
so we,

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.610
about two months ago switched

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.098
from,

00:04:48.098 --> 00:04:49.681
- Longer than that.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.240
- About three or four months ago?

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.350
About three or four months
ago, we switched from

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.240
heroin to Fentanyl.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.523
So we do straight Fentanyl
now, not any heroin.

00:05:02.027 --> 00:05:03.877
And Fentanyl is a lot more expensive.

00:05:05.057 --> 00:05:09.576
And so we probably
spend 150 to $200 a day.

00:05:09.576 --> 00:05:11.820
- [Mark] What's the difference in terms

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.560
of the high that you get from Fentanyl?

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.533
- It's basically the same high,

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.570
except Fentanyl is

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:24.440
much, much more dangerous
and a lot more lethal,

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.543
a lot more potent.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.653
They say Fentanyl is like 10
times stronger than heroin.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:31.963
So,

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.720
we actually both got off using a needle,

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.350
because of doing Fentanyl.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.563
Because we don't have to shoot it anymore,

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.323
but...

00:05:43.323 --> 00:05:44.156
- [Mark] Do you smoke it?

00:05:44.156 --> 00:05:45.860
- Yeah. We smoke it.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.823
So that's kind of a good thing, but,

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.490
yeah, you get, you know,

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:54.273
very drowsy or, you're not off,

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:56.813
you know.

00:05:56.813 --> 00:05:58.790
Because of our tolerance we sometimes

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.963
really gain energy from it.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:07.743
But yeah, we usually spend
around 150 to $200 a day on,

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.160
on Fentanyl.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.910
- [Mark] Is it for the pair
of you or for each of you?

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:12.930
- Yeah, no. For the,

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.530
for the both of us.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:17.943
Basically it's the same
routine every single day,

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.360
living down here, we wake up,

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.770
we hopefully still have

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.853
drugs leftover from the night before.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.880
You know, we do what we can to stay well.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.550
And then we go to work.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:34.053
And work being, we go boost.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.270
Because we don't have a car or anything,

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:40.633
we have to use public
transportation, which,

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:42.733
you know,

00:06:42.733 --> 00:06:44.840
takes the majority of the time,

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:46.490
your time.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.000
So we spend like, you
know, six to eight hours

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.203
out boosting and getting money,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.150
cashing that,

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.453
that merchandise in.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:06:59.680
And then we

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.683
go pick up,

00:07:02.228 --> 00:07:03.910
and go back to our tent,

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:04.743
and get high.

00:07:04.743 --> 00:07:06.400
It's the same thing every single day.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.323
- [Mark] Who do you
sell the merchandise to?

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.043
- We sell it to different people.

00:07:13.188 --> 00:07:14.021
- [Mark] There,

00:07:14.021 --> 00:07:14.854
there are people who will pay...

00:07:14.854 --> 00:07:15.690
- Yeah.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:18.580
So, out in Los Angeles,

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.100
it's not like this where I'm from,

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.480
or where she's from,

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.980
but there's, you know,

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.190
there's a lot of people out here.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.570
There's a lot of

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.770
different opportunities out here.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:31.540
Whether that be good opportunities
or bad opportunities.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.413
And,

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.410
you know, you can basically

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:40.093
do a wide variety of things to get money.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.570
And so there's

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:47.400
also a wide variety of
people that are willing to

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.810
cash in on

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.520
your addiction,

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.800
basically, you know?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.210
And so you have a lot of

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:59.170
kids out here that are
addicted to drugs that

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:00.390
do whatever they have to

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.660
to get high every day and stay well.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.947
And there's people out there that

00:08:06.947 --> 00:08:08.980
take advantage of that.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.333
And so,

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.490
yeah, there's,

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.340
not just one or two, there's many, many

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.560
many people that buy

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.870
the merchandise out here.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.940
- [Mark] Now, being a
white couple on the street,

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.120
you're, almost like a target

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:22.953
for a lot of

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.560
people in this neighborhood.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.460
- Yeah, for sure.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.410
- [Mark] Have you experienced...

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.243
- Yeah, for sure.

00:08:29.243 --> 00:08:30.823
When we first got down here,

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.030
you know we,

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.343
didn't know anybody.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.810
Obviously being young and white,

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.593
were very much targeted.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.490
They automatically assume
we have a lot of money.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.400
They automatically assume that

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.550
they pretty much can
manipulate us in any way,

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.040
to get what they want out of us.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.993
So when we first moved down here,

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.680
we were introduced to a guy,

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.940
and,

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:02.900
he,

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:04.100
basically

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.933
was

00:09:04.933 --> 00:09:06.073
helping us,

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.360
you know,

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.363
he let us stay in his tent
with him for about a month.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:13.733
He was,

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:15.663
you know,

00:09:15.663 --> 00:09:17.418
getting us by every day.

00:09:17.418 --> 00:09:19.040
(loud Mexican music coming from outside)

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:19.873
And we,

00:09:19.873 --> 00:09:21.950
because we were so new, we weren't

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:25.030
we didn't know the ulterior motives behind

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:26.360
him doing that.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.970
And so, we thought

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.220
he was just a good guy,

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.370
and being naive, you know,

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.083
people that we were at first,

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.610
we continued to let him help us.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.503
And, when we decided to leave him,

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.310
like leave living with him.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.503
He got very, very upset.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.433
He said, we owed him money.

00:09:50.975 --> 00:09:52.250
And so he came

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:54.463
and found us,

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.500
was very, very angry,

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.990
he was yelling and had a giant metal pole

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.030
and actually hit Megan

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.280
like three or four times
with the metal pole.

00:10:09.492 --> 00:10:10.903
And then when I came back,

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:15.390
he was still yelling and screaming,

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.383
and he hit me a few times,

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:23.050
but we ultimately had to pay $500 to

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.074
get out of this situation.

00:10:25.074 --> 00:10:25.907
- He extorted us.

00:10:25.907 --> 00:10:27.960
- He extorted us.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.400
And that's not

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.760
an uncommon thing down here, you know?

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.070
And,

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.223
luckily,

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.943
I was able to get that kind of money.

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.263
My parents were very,

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.233
worrisome,

00:10:43.233 --> 00:10:46.803
and wondering why I needed so much money,

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.040
but, we did get the money,

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.233
we got through it.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.800
And ever since then, we've been a lot more

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.520
alert and aware of everything
going on around us.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:03.810
And so luckily we haven't
let that come in between us.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:04.643
You know...

00:11:05.492 --> 00:11:06.550
- [Mark] How old are you guys?

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:08.250
- [Matt] Both of us just turned 29.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.050
- [Mark] Have you been
in jail for boosting

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:10.883
or any other thing?

00:11:10.883 --> 00:11:12.535
- [Matt] Yeah. I,

00:11:12.535 --> 00:11:13.600
I actually,

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.660
I've been to jail twice

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.280
since we've been down here.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:22.220
The first time I went to jail for 19 days.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.193
And then the second
time I went to jail for,

00:11:27.504 --> 00:11:28.810
like, a month.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.724
And she was but...

00:11:30.724 --> 00:11:31.557
(Megan whispering)

00:11:31.557 --> 00:11:33.170
- [Matt] That was first time...

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:36.793
- And she was, she was out
here by herself both times,

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.250
you know, which is very, very

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.720
scary for me.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.720
Because I know

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.040
what she has to deal with every day.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:51.070
And also when I go to jail

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:54.460
and my mind clears up from all
the drugs and everything else

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.160
